WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.721
When the network fails, an emergency turns into silence.

2
00:00:04.071 --> 00:00:05.949
SENDA keeps the message moving.

3
00:00:07.349 --> 00:00:10.741
An SOS with voice does not fit in one satellite message.

4
00:00:11.091 --> 00:00:15.101
SENDA splits it into twelve shards across satellite, LoRa and Iridium.

5
00:00:15.451 --> 00:00:20.081
No channel can do it alone. Together, ninety-nine percent, computed exactly.

6
00:00:21.481 --> 00:00:24.382
A neighbour or a drone carries it, and cannot read it.

7
00:00:24.732 --> 00:00:27.548
Change a single byte, and the recipient rejects it.

8
00:00:28.948 --> 00:00:30.825
No camera can see through a wall.

9
00:00:31.175 --> 00:00:35.655
SENDA fuses replies, phones, breathing detected over Wi-Fi, and knocking.

10
00:00:36.005 --> 00:00:39.888
And it only says ninety-eight percent when two independent sources agree.

11
00:00:41.288 --> 00:00:44.744
In a wildfire, the fire front is computed from wind and slope.

12
00:00:45.094 --> 00:00:47.313
What is new is crossing it with the masts.

13
00:00:47.663 --> 00:00:54.660
Here, the mast falls fifty-three minutes before the warning deadline. The alert must go out earlier, or over no-network channels.

14
00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:01.500
At Adamuz, according to a Guardia Civil report, the track gave a signal twenty-two hours earlier.

15
00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:06.138
SENDA compares each circuit with its own history and proposes an inspection.

16
00:01:06.488 --> 00:01:08.579
This is data that already exists.

17
00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:13.200
And there is always a satellite passing: the router knows when.

18
00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.013
All of this runs today, offline, in the browser and on Android.

19
00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:23.270
One hundred and eight automated tests and twenty-five real-browser tests verify it.

20
00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:29.278
What is missing is the field: pilots with civil protection, rail and firefighters.

21
00:01:29.628 --> 00:01:31.633
SENDA. Offline first, for sure.
